Get high-quality gear and furniture reliably: work on quality items and buildings is set aside at the last moment and finished by your best (or inspired) pawn.

[h1]Crafting[/h1]
[list]
[*] Pauses quality bill work the instant before completion; the item is set aside (haulable, shelvable) until a qualifying colonist exists to complete the job. If the current crafter already qualifies, their work completion is not interrupted.
[*] [b]Shared unfinished work:[/b] bills are no longer locked to the pawn who started an item, so anyone can resume work on an unfinished item. This also rescues items whose creator died.
[*] [b]Per-bill conditions[/b] (minimum skill, require inspiration, require production specialist) with a live quality-odds preview for your configuration and current best crafter.
[*] Once a crafter is identified that can complete the work, a bill assigned to that pawn is created automatically (and removed when completed).
[*] [b]Stock caps per product:[/b] stop starting new items once enough are waiting for a finisher; in-progress items still get completed.
[/list]

[h1]Construction[/h1]
[list]
[*] Opt in per building via the [i]Quality Job[/i] button on any quality blueprint or frame, or globally for all quality buildings from mod settings. Enablement is implicit: set any option and the build is managed; the [i]Clear[/i] button resets it.
[*] [b]Per-build conditions[/b] (minimum skill, require inspiration, require production specialist, retry until quality level reached) with a live quality-odds preview for your configuration and current best builder.
[*] [b]Target quality:[/b] builds that roll below your chosen quality are automatically marked for deconstruction and will be rebuilt until you get the desired quality (or you clear the build from being a Quality Job).
[*] Managed builds pause at 100% and wait for a builder who meets your conditions; a sparkle overlay marks them on the map.
[/list]

[h1]Worth Knowing[/h1]
[list]
[*] This mod isn't a cheat that gives you better quality items. Quality is rolled by the pawn who finishes the work, and this mod just helps ensure that is someone with a high success rate.
[*] Inspired Creativity is consumed on the finishing touch, exactly as vanilla intends.
[*] Paused items show [i]Author: reserved (Quality Jobs)[/i] and cannot be resumed until a qualifying pawn exists.
[*] Ideology's production specialist role is supported but not required; no DLC is needed.
[/list]

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]
[list]
[*] Multiplayer compatible (RimWorld Multiplayer).
[*] Safe to add/remove mid-game, but removal without disabling in mod settings will leave unfinished items without an owner (they must be cancelled). Disabling the mod makes items resumable by their (new) owner.
[*] No defs are patched and unmanaged bills/builds behave exactly as vanilla; integration is a handful of targeted Harmony patches at job boundaries.
[*] [b]Designed for Performance:[/b] Extensive caching, rendering from pre-calculated caches, scoped invalidation, no per-tick logic.
[*] Requires Harmony.
[/list]

Found a bug or an incompatible mod? Let me know in the comments.

